      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Car Transport From Gorakhpur To Delhi</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a vehicle arrives at its destination, the delivery handover process must be conducted with precision to guarantee the integrity of the shipment and the satisfaction of both the carrier and the consignee. The procedure begins with a daylight condition re‑inspection that compares the car’s exterior and interior against the original pickup photographs.</p>
<p>This visual audit verifies that no new damage has occurred during transit and confirms that all accessories and parts remain intact.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Photographic Comparison:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The consignee’s inspector opens the original image set from the pickup station and scrolls through each shot, checking for scratches, dents, and other defects. Any discrepancy is noted and photographed for documentation.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Lighting and Angle Checks:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The inspector ensures that the current lighting matches the original conditions by using a standard light source and capturing images from the same angles to facilitate an accurate side‑by‑side comparison.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Interior Verification:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Seats, carpeting, dashboard, and electronic controls are inspected for wear, tears, or malfunctioning components, and any issues are logged.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Following the visual assessment, the odometer reading is verified against the LR bilty. The LR bilty contains the recorded mileage at the point of departure.</p>
<p>The inspector reads the vehicle’s odometer, compares the figure to the bilty, and confirms that the difference falls within the acceptable variance range set by the carrier. Any discrepancy triggers an immediate investigation and may result in a revised bill of lading or a claim.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer Reading:</strong> The inspector records the current mileage on a checklist and notes the date and time of verification.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Variance Analysis:</strong> The difference between the bilty and the current reading is calculated. A variance of up to 5 miles is typically acceptable; beyond that, a detailed report is required.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Documentation:</strong> Both the bilty and the new reading are scanned and attached to the digital delivery file for audit purposes.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>Once visual and mileage checks are complete, the final step is the signed condition sign‑off. The consignee’s representative signs the delivery receipt, acknowledging that the vehicle meets the agreed condition and that the odometer reading is accurate.</p>
<p>The carrier’s inspector also signs, confirming that all documentation has been verified. Both signatures are timestamped, and the signed receipt is stored electronically in the carrier’s system, completing the delivery handover.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



